to be affecting our rounding.

00:15:46.574 --> 00:15:52.515
So we'll take this, we'll take that eight,
round it up, and our final answer is going

00:15:52.515 --> 00:15:57.944
to be 2.9, showing those two sig figs.

00:15:58.665 --> 00:16:01.155
And as you're kind of going
through these, if there's units

00:16:01.155 --> 00:16:02.685
involved, we would keep them.

00:16:02.714 --> 00:16:02.984
Oops.

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:06.089
And we would put them in
our final answer as well.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:08.400
So that's one of the things
that we're gonna be looking at.

00:16:08.459 --> 00:16:13.680
Let's do one last example of combined
operations with units to show

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:15.569
all of it together with rounding.

00:16:15.780 --> 00:16:18.810
So on this last example, what
we're going to be actually

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.540
looking at is this problem above.

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:27.360
So what we can see is that there is a
very big problem with multiple steps

00:16:27.365 --> 00:16:29.550
in it, many different types of units.

00:16:29.999 --> 00:16:37.079
So what we have above is 12.489
centimeters minus 4.234 centimeters times

00:16:37.079 --> 00:16:41.939
30.72 kilograms divided by 25.5 seconds.

00:16:42.359 --> 00:16:43.439
Oh, that's a lot.

00:16:43.859 --> 00:16:45.209
So we gotta remember our units.

00:16:45.209 --> 00:16:47.099
That was the one of the
big tips I put here.

00:16:47.489 --> 00:16:52.529
So let's do the first part, which
is parentheses, so we can do

00:16:52.529 --> 00:16:55.889
the parentheses, we can subtract
because they are the same units.

00:16:56.449 --> 00:17:06.149
So when we do that, what we're going to
get is 8.255 centimeters times that 30.72

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:12.270
kilograms divided by that 25.5 seconds.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.819
And I'm gonna leave that in
parentheses so you can kind of

00:17:14.819 --> 00:17:16.680
remember where that came from.

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:20.040
Now one thing we have to do
is keep track of sig figs.

00:17:20.459 --> 00:17:24.419
So you can see we have 1, 2,
3 sig figs for each of those

00:17:24.419 --> 00:17:26.040
values after the decimal.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:30.480
So that means that this one did not
get affected at all from our rounding.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:33.179
So we're gonna cut leave it at
that point, so we know that it's

00:17:33.179 --> 00:17:34.409
gonna be three after the decimal.

00:17:34.409 --> 00:17:37.050
So, okay, so that's
good to know for later.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:41.669
The next step is, remember that
I said that everything that is in

00:17:41.760 --> 00:17:47.370
the denominator, in the numerator,
assume that they are in parentheses.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.510
So we're gonna assume the top.

00:17:49.064 --> 00:17:50.924
And the bottom are in parentheses.

00:17:51.104 --> 00:17:55.454
So we're gonna do our order of operation
or multiplication on top first.

00:17:56.024 --> 00:18:03.074
So when we take 8.255 times
30.72, we are going to get

00:18:03.194 --> 00:18:13.184
253.5936 divided by 25.5 seconds.

00:18:13.784 --> 00:18:16.154
So that would've been
the next part, right?

00:18:16.154 --> 00:18:18.194
That would've been your multiplication.

00:18:19.695 --> 00:18:21.764
I'm gonna write this, label those for us.

00:18:23.175 --> 00:18:27.254
So when we do that step, what we
have to do is counter sig figs again.

00:18:27.675 --> 00:18:34.455
So what we have is four sig figs on the
left and four sig figs on the right.

00:18:34.459 --> 00:18:38.385
So we're still right around that
same point, still at four sig figs.

00:18:39.374 --> 00:18:45.794
Our next portion is divide, which when
we have these two values, so we have

00:18:45.794 --> 00:18:48.195
our four sig figs from the top number.

00:18:48.794 --> 00:18:53.475
Then we have a total of
three sig figs on the bottom.

00:18:54.345 --> 00:18:58.335
What this tells us is finally we have a
number that's gonna affect our sig figs.

00:18:59.085 --> 00:19:03.764
So we are going to have three
sig figs as our final answer.

00:19:03.794 --> 00:19:07.695
So when we carry that out,
remember we save rounding for last.

00:19:07.695 --> 00:19:10.784
So I'm just gonna write every value
that we have on our calculator.

00:19:11.504 --> 00:19:15.945
So we have 9.44847.

00:19:17.639 --> 00:19:22.170
When we are doing that as well, we should
also be keeping our units in here, which

00:19:22.170 --> 00:19:24.600
I realized mine kind of disappeared.

00:19:25.860 --> 00:19:29.550
So on the step before centimeters and
